Let $X$ be the set of $p$-tuples $(g_1, ..., g_p)$ whose product is $e$. The cyclic group $C_p$ acts by cyclic rotation. There are $abs(G)^(p-1)$ such tuples, and each orbit has size $1$ or $p$ by orbit-stabiliser. The number $l$ of orbits of size $1$ is divisible by $p$, while $(e, ..., e)$ gives $l >= 1$. Hence another constant tuple $(g, ..., g)$ occurs with $g != e$. It belongs to $X$, so $g^p = e$, and therefore $o(g) = p$.
